drm/msm/dpu: use the real DSC output buffer size on SM4450

The DSC block on SM4450 has a 600-byte output buffer per encoder, but
_dsc_calc_output_buf_max_addr() reports 2400 / num_softslice, i.e. four times
the hardware capacity. The rate buffer therefore over-reports how much
compressed data it can hold, the encoder keeps producing data that the block
cannot buffer, and the emitted stream is corrupt: the panel decodes structured
noise whose layout follows the DSC slice geometry (the artifact moves when
slice_width / slice_count / slice_per_pkt change, and nothing is reported on
the DSI link because the corruption happens before the PHY).

With the correct size the Xiaomi "m19" panel on the Redmi 12 5G (SM4450)
produces a correct image.

The value should eventually come from the DPU catalog instead of a machine
compatibility check; this keeps the bring-up patch small.

Signed-off-by: sky-linux bring-up <orange200213@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_dsc_1_2.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_dsc_1_2.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_dsc_1_2.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_dsc_1_2.c
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <drm/drm_managed.h>
 
 #include <drm/display/drm_dsc_helper.h>
@@ -65,6 +66,12 @@ static int _dsc_calc_output_buf_max_addr(struct dpu_hw_dsc *hw_dsc, int num_softs
 	if (hw_dsc->caps->features & BIT(DPU_DSC_NATIVE_42x_EN))
 		max_addr /= 2;
 
+	/* SM4450 exposes a 600-byte DSC rate buffer, not 2400 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,sm4450")) {
+		max_addr = 600 / num_softslice;
+		pr_info("sky-dsc-buffer: max_addr=%d slices=%d\n",
+			max_addr - 1, num_softslice);
+	}
+
 	return max_addr - 1;
 };
